        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Install ClawHub packages for new Claw agents",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- preflight each exact, version-pinned ClawHub package as install or reuse and bind that owner decision into the consented plan\n- revalidate plugin owner state immediately before mutation, then use the existing skill and plugin installer surfaces\n- persist pending, complete, or failed package provenance so partial installs and independently owned packages remain explainable\n- return structured partial results when a package or later agent/config mutation fails after package work has begun\n- warn across CLI, Gateway, and Control UI plugin removal when any Claw provenance, including uncertain provenance, references the plugin\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the package-owner slice of the experimental Claw lifecycle. It keeps the grouped RFC contract (`packages[].kind`, `source`, `ref`, and exact `version`) and deliberately does not restore generic artifact selectors or agent skill lists. MCP servers and cron jobs remain blocked for later stack slices.\n\nThe dry-run records whether each package is absent or already present at the exact version. Apply requires the matching plan digest and rechecks plugin owner state before invoking the installer, so a package cannot silently change from Claw-installed to independently owned, or the reverse, after consent. Package work runs before agent/config/workspace mutation; any later collision returns a partial result that retains the package evidence.\n\nPackage references describe dependency provenance, not exclusive ownership. An exact package reused from the operator is recorded as independently owned. A Claw-started install is recorded before external mutation and transitions from pending to complete or failed. Existing experimental databases receive the new update timestamp through an additive migration. Plugin uninstall remains operator-controlled but warns for complete and uncertain Claw references.\n\nThe CLI remains process-gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1` in the base of this stack.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #101973 managed workspace files\n- This PR: package owner preflight, installers, provenance, and shared uninstall warnings\n- Next: #102296 status and remove\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:src`\n- focused Oxlint on changed Claw, plugin, and state files\n- 47 focused package, provenance, plugin-uninstall, and state-database tests\n- 6 Claw lifecycle E2E tests\n- `codex-review --mode local` clean after addressing additive migration, error preservation, and uncertain-reference warning findings\n",
